ies make the shape that of a random binary search tree, whatever order the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements arrive in, so lookup, insertion and removal take O(log ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"text":") expected time. A treap","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"also splits at an element into the elements below it and the rest, and joins two treaps whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements don’t interleave. The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indexed by rank like an array: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"treap[0]"},{"text":" is the smallest element. Reading an element by index","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"costs O(log ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":") expected, and a pass through the whole collection costs O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var numbers: Treap = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","let parts = numbers.split(at: 5)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [1, 3]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [5, 8, 9]","var rejoined = parts.lower","try rejoined.join(parts.upper)","rejoined == numbers           \/\/ true"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The priorities come from a random number generator given at creation,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SystemRandomNumberGenerator"},{"text":" by default; a seeded generator makes every shape reproducible.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The treap draws one seed from it and keeps its own generator state, so a copy draws the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"priorities as its original.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inl